    "rules_correction": [
      {
        "id": "B:resolution_exile_cost_success",
        "old_claim": "A prevented cost must not queue the reflexive trigger.",
        "corrected": "True prohibition/no legal resource prevents paying. A legal payment modified by replacement, including replaced event, is still paid under118.11;118.12 tracks the choice to pay. Do not conflate with actual-effect mill event success. Root agreed."
      }
    ],
    "source_discrepancies": [
      {
        "card": "Rite of Renewal",
        "source": "TargetPlayerShufflesTargetCardsEffect.apply",
        "detail": "Java returns without shuffling if chosen-card set is empty; Oracle instructs targeted player to shuffle even for zero cards. Rust proof must require the shuffle."
      },
      {
        "card": "New Way Forward",
        "source": "TargetSource.possibleTargets",
        "detail": "Java broadly enumerates all graveyard/exile cards. CR609.7a restricts departed objects to those referred to by stack/replacement/prevention/delayed objects. Rust must use the current rule source set, including permanent-spell continuation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "implementation": [
    "CreatureSpells and SpellSubtypeAny typed restrictions evaluate the selected spell face; all activation/other purposes reject; ordinary owned mana lots remain valid after producer departure.",
    "Mass copy snapshots one copiable recipe and all other currently controlled creature incarnations before applying existing EOT copy layers, with no entry events or counter copying.",
    "GraveyardOwnerOfPlayerGroup binds graveyard cards to the chosen player at announcement and resolution. A dedicated aggregate shuffle instruction keeps all role groups and shuffles the player even if zero selected cards remain.",
    "DoubleEnteredCreatureDamage uses existing exact turn-entry history and current/LKI DamageSource facts/controller. Departures no longer erase this sparse history; ordinary begin_turn clears it. Reentry uses a different ObjectRef. No new hot state field.",
    "Pure exile-loop proof already excludes replacement/zone/copy/grant/control observers and only admits three noncreature pure exilers plus inert lands. Normalize only participant history to baseline, after verifying all unrelated history is identical. Inert departed entry history supplies no legal escape. The previous underflow-based stale-history negative is now the distinguishing draw positive; its original source remains pinned by the baseline. Explicit Neriv observer and existing optional/observer negatives still reject a draw.",
    "Resolution ExileGraveyard cost candidates reject true graveyard-exile prohibition. Existing optional payment and independently targeted reflexive packet handle Kishla. Legal replacement-modified payments stay paid under CR118.11/12; do not infer success from actual zone movement.",
    "Existing Narset May + DiscardHand + resolution-time actual cast-count draw works with an empty hand; declining is independent."
  ],
